  "solution": {
    "text": "This is a heterogeneous equilibrium. The equilibrium constant for it can be written as:<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mi></mi><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo> </mrow> <mi>c</mi> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>CO</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math><br /><br />The concentration of CaCO<sub>3</sub>&nbsp;and CaO are assumed to be constant as they are present as solid.<br /><br />Hence, CaCO<sub>3</sub> has no effect on equilibrium concentration."
  }
